commit 8eaeccbd9dc346cb884a6270a39dfc36735c7964
Author: Javier Calvarro Nelson <jacalvar@microsoft.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 13 09:40:52 2026 +0200

    [Blazor] Support Aspire Dashboard on Native AOT (#68307)
    
    * Enable minimal Blazor Server Native AOT path
    
    Keep reflection as the compatibility path while generating fixed server marker contracts, retaining outbound JS result types, and allowing apps to supply JS interop JSON metadata.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Support Blazor Web root operations in Native AOT
    
    Generate the fixed root-operation JSON contracts used by blazor.web.js and remove the form-binding-only change from this experiment.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Cover Aspire Dashboard Native AOT JSON paths
    
    Compose application JSON contracts into protected browser storage and generate the fixed NavigationOptions contract used by Server navigation.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Support interactive forms in Native AOT
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Cover remaining Dashboard Native AOT runtime JSON paths
    
    Use generated framework contracts for modules and persistent state, and provide converter-backed JS interop metadata without reflection serialization.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    Copilot-Session: 19dd876d-31dc-41b4-a53b-aa2299746d2a
    
    * Test configured JSON metadata resolution
    
    Validate framework JSON metadata through the configured JsonSerializerOptions resolver chain instead of invoking individual resolvers directly.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    Copilot-Session: 22ea1330-4e21-4ac3-ab94-eafa89a2efc6
    
    * Add Native AOT Blazor browser coverage
    
    Exercise reflection-enabled Interactive Server paths used by the Aspire Dashboard with the current Components Testing Native AOT harness.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    Copilot-Session: 19dd876d-31dc-41b4-a53b-aa2299746d2a
    
    * Fix Native AOT test CI integration
    
    Keep ordinary restores off unpublished shared-framework runtime packs, restore the Native AOT fixture with matching harness properties, and tolerate JS interop completion races after cancellation.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Narrow Native AOT fixture diagnostics
    
    Root only the application assembly and keep the reflection-enabled fixture's reachable trim and AOT diagnostics as warnings under CI.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Keep fixture pruning diagnostics as warnings
    
    Allow known NU1510 package-pruning diagnostics from existing framework projects during the Native AOT fixture restore without suppressing them.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Fix Native AOT fixture restore graph
    
    Let the app's RuntimeIdentifiers prepare RID assets without imposing a RID on analyzer projects, and flow known NU1510 pruning diagnostics across referenced restores.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    * Isolate Native AOT fixture restore
    
    Restore only the fixture root with AOT properties so parallel CI builds do not rewrite shared transitive project assets.
    
    Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
    
    ---------
    
